                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;h2&gt;1.1.2 (2025-07-15)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bugs Fixed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Name&lt;/code&gt; property of &lt;code&gt;TableService&lt;/code&gt; now always has the value of &lt;code&gt;default&lt;/code&gt; since this is its only valid value. Fixes &lt;a href="https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/issues/51210" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/issues/51210/hovercard"&gt;#51210&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/releases/tag/System.ClientModel_1.5.1"&gt;System.ClientModel_1.5.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;h2&gt;1.5.1 (2025-07-14)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bugs Fixed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed an issue where System.ClientModel.SourceGeneration was running slowly for large projects with many dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Breaking Changes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The System.ClientModel.SourceGeneration used to auto-discover &lt;code&gt;IJsonModel&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;'s that were in the project as well as any types &lt;code&gt;T&lt;/code&gt; used in &lt;code&gt;ModelReaderWriter.Read&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ModelReaderWriter.Write&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.  Now you must explicitly add a &lt;code&gt;ModelReaderWriterBuildableAttribute&lt;/code&gt; with each type that needs to have AOT friendly reading and writing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
